<pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I1b998258a1e828f76487dfad4af99abba65e4753" commit="aeca8315866221575442af6bfcd61008be8a489f" commit_message="Revert &quot;[Autotest]Collect adb logs for SimpleConnect&quot;  This reverts commit ab25b93c9b00a0bdacef99da61aed0f1343943fc.  According to crbug.com/551117, ADB logs are now collected properly.  BUG=chromium:621146 TEST=network_WiFi_SimpleConnect  Change-Id: I1b998258a1e828f76487dfad4af99abba65e4753 Signed-off-by: Brian Norris &lt;briannorris@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/706095 " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="706095" owner_email="briannorris@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/third_party/autotest" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/autotest" ref="refs/changes/95/706095/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="If328e9c9467c3a870391916bc244dda1817a4356" commit="95b4c7ccf3d414a4865d360cdb6e76058dab4037" commit_message="site_linux_system: drop require caps 'fatal_failure'  This isn't used, and we should be minimizing use of TestFail for issues that are unrelated to the actual DUT state -- e.g., missing router capabilities. If the test infrastructure is really bad, we should probably use TestError.  BUG=none TEST=wifi_matfunc  Change-Id: If328e9c9467c3a870391916bc244dda1817a4356 Signed-off-by: Brian Norris &lt;briannorris@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/706096 Reviewed-by: Edward Hill &lt;ecgh@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="706096" owner_email="briannorris@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="3" project="chromiumos/third_party/autotest" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/autotest" ref="refs/changes/96/706096/3" remote="cros" total_fail_count="2"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I3a912fb759b9e59abd5ca18d3dc0ede5fd638067" commit="2a610077956edb4a9dddd39ab0f22d469058f9b1" commit_message="wifi_test_context_manager: log signal level when connected  Test lab issues can show up as poorly-connected networks, with very low signal strength. Sometimes, we may even be associated only briefly, and the DUT immediately disconnects. Logging the signal level is a simple addition to our understanding of failures; it can show if we have a marginal connection, and it might even help make a quick-disconnect more obvious (it will print 'None').  BUG=none TEST=network_WiFi_SimpleConnect.XXX on flaky wifi cells  Change-Id: I3a912fb759b9e59abd5ca18d3dc0ede5fd638067 Signed-off-by: Brian Norris &lt;briannorris@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/706116 Reviewed-by: Edward Hill &lt;ecgh@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Kirtika Ruchandani &lt;kirtika@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="706116" owner_email="briannorris@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/third_party/autotest" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/autotest" ref="refs/changes/16/706116/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I7bece2ea623f8a40f92c2ab230df08157eb3b19b" commit="8989f420f64d5aabca903c7c36f328ba13d7eaca" commit_message="libc++: Install libc++ libraries during setup_board.  To be able to build packages with libc++, libc++ libraries must be installed during setup_board stage.  BUG=chromium:724628 TEST=./setup_board --board={daisy/peppy} installed libc++ libraries. CQ-DEPEND=CL:710216  Change-Id: I7bece2ea623f8a40f92c2ab230df08157eb3b19b Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/574646 Commit-Ready: Manoj Gupta &lt;manojgupta@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Manoj Gupta &lt;manojgupta@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Mike Frysinger &lt;vapier@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="1" gerrit_number="574646" owner_email="manojgupta@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="6" project="chromiumos/platform/crosutils" projec